# 4. Claim

This is the first serious scholarly abstraction.

```text
PASSAGES
   ↓
CLAIM
```

Example:

```text
CLAIM C-143

Abhinavagupta treats recognition as
re-identification rather than acquisition
of genuinely new knowledge.
```

Expose:

```text
claim
scope
modality
source passages
supporting evidence
counterevidence
interpretive status
authority
```

Crucially:

```text
SOURCE-SAYS
SCHOLAR-RECONSTRUCTS
PĀṬALA-INFERS
```

must remain visibly distinct.

Checkpoint:

```text
C0 proposed
C1 evidence attached
C2 scope/modality audit
C3 contradiction search
C4 independent review
C5 adjudicated
```

