# 6. Crux

I would absolutely expose this as its own product.

A crux is:

> the smallest unresolved proposition whose resolution would materially change the debate.

```text
CRUX-23

Question:
Does Utpaladeva require enduring subject identity?

Position A
Position B

decisive evidence required
current best evidence
downstream consequences
```

This is vastly more useful than another 8,000-word literature review.

Checkpoint:

```text
CR0 candidate
CR1 downstream sensitivity confirmed
CR2 rivals represented
CR3 decisive-evidence conditions defined
CR4 reviewed
```

Product:

> **Open Crux**

This could become a major scholar-acquisition mechanism.

