# 8. Scholar Attestation

This is probably the highest-moat product after Translation Proof.

A scholar should not need to “approve all of Pāṭala.”

They attest to something precise:

```text
Scholar Attestation

Scholar: X
Target: TranslationRevision T17
Statement:
  "I have reviewed the Sanskrit-to-English
   translation for semantic fidelity."

Scope:
  verses 1.5.1–1.5.15

Verdict:
  ACCEPT WITH QUALIFICATIONS
```

Attestation types:

```text
source authenticity
textual reading
translation fidelity
historical claim
argument reconstruction
bibliographic completeness
```

Checkpoint:

```text
SA0 invitation
SA1 review submitted
SA2 identity verified
SA3 attestation signed
SA4 public/citable
```

This is what eventually creates the **expert verification network**.

