# 12. Education / Understanding Check

This is one of the most distinctive products.

Compile arguments into questions where answering correctly demonstrates the relevant conceptual distinction.

Example:

```text
Question:
Which proposition would Utpaladeva
have to reject for argument ARG-32
to fail?

A ...
B ...
C ...
D ...
```

Each distractor maps to a specific error:

```text
scope confusion
modal confusion
premise/conclusion reversal
rival-position confusion
```

Product outputs:

```text
MCQ
argument completion
premise ranking
contradiction spotting
source attribution
counterfactual questions
```

Checkpoint:

```text
ED0 generated
ED1 answer proof
ED2 distractor proof
ED3 ambiguity test
ED4 learner calibration
ED5 reviewed
```

That's far better than generic quizzes.

