# The first focused checkpoints I would build

Don't attempt all products simultaneously.

I'd make **six canonical vertical products** first:

```text
CP1 — PASSAGE
source + canonical IDs + morphology/readings

CP2 — TRANSLATION PROOF
translation + multidimensional proof

CP3 — CLAIM
passage → defensible proposition

CP4 — ARGUMENT
claims → inference + validity + defeaters

CP5 — SCHOLAR REVIEW
review + attestation + correction history

CP6 — RESEARCH PACKET
compile all of the above into a useful deliverable
```

Then:

```text
CP7 — SYNTHESIS
CP8 — ESSAY
CP9 — EDUCATION
CP10 — BENCHMARK
```

That order matters.

Because everything after CP6 becomes a **projection** of the first six rather than a separate AI capability.

